# AI-Assisted Function Point Analysis

## Short Description

AI-Assisted Function Point Analysis uses artificial intelligence to support the discovery, identification and classification of business functionality within software systems.

The objective is not to replace analysts, but to accelerate system understanding, reduce manual effort and improve consistency.

Within P21, AI-assisted FPA is primarily used as a system discovery technique.

---

## Why Use AI?

Traditional Function Point Analysis often requires:

- application knowledge
- business knowledge
- source code analysis
- database analysis
- document review

AI can accelerate these activities by helping identify:

- business functions
- transactions
- data entities
- application boundaries
- dependencies

